PPU reservation registration is idempotent for stable context slots.

Repeated thread-slot reuse previously consumed the fixed 128-entry registry,
leaving later distinct contexts outside reservation invalidation. Serialize
registration, deduplicate before capacity use, and publish initialized entries
with a release count observed by every reader with acquire semantics. Genuine
distinct-context overflow fails explicitly; the capacity is unchanged.

